    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\n`mini.surround`\n\n### Description\n\nIt would be great to have a configuration option of making `sf` and `sF` in `mini.surround` non dot-repeatable (or by using `;` and `,` as in fFtT). Oftentimes I find myself wanting to replace a lot of surrounds in a file, so I repeatedly call `sf` and `sr`. But after each call of `sf` I loose what is stored in `.`",
    "closed_at": "2024-10-15T16:58:53Z",
