    "comment_data": [
        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the suggestion!\r\n\r\nI do agree that having movement (and highlighting `sh` operator, for that matter) be dot-repeatable was not the best choice. As the realization that dot-repeatable should be only editing operation came far later than when 'mini.surround' was implemented.\r\n\r\nThat said, I am fairly hesitant on making a breaking change here. I'll think about it.\r\n\r\n------\r\n\r\nOne thing to note about the specific example in the issue is that calling `sf` is not needed for `sr` to work. They share exactly the same logic of finding which surrounding will be replaced. So calling only `sr` should be enough here.",
