            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "just want to pitch in. on the mini.surround README.md the video and under the features section it still says ALL actions are dot repeatable.\n\nthis had me fooled for bout an hour trying to figure out why i cant dot repeat 'sf' :D thought it might be useful but i understand why you chose to take it out.\n\ni could PR and change it linking back to this issue if you want (obviously not the video just text), but up to you.\n\n```\nFeatures\nActions (all of them are dot-repeatable out of the box and respect v:count for searching surrounding) with configurable keymappings:\nAdd surrounding with sa (in visual mode or on motion).\nDelete surrounding with sd.\nReplace surrounding with sr.\nFind surrounding with sf or sF (move cursor right or left).\nHighlight surrounding with sh.\nChange number of neighbor lines with sn (see |MiniSurround-algorithm|).\n```",
