        {
            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "Following up here since the original comment also asks about using `;` and `,` for repeating movement actions, which _is_ a common pattern. I'd like to add this behavior using the treesitter textobjs extension's [move capabilities](https://github.com/nvim-treesitter/nvim-treesitter-textobjects?tab=readme-ov-file#text-objects-move) (search: \"from another plugin\"), but `MiniSurround.find()` is not very well documented, and there doesn't seem to be a `.find_left()` method any more.",
