        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> ... also asks about using ; and , for repeating movement actions, which is a common pattern ...\n\nAlthough common, it is mostly reserved for `fFtT`. Especially in 'mini.nvim' via 'mini.jump'. See #1077 for more details (which *mighty* get implemented one day, maybe).\n\n> ... but MiniSurround.find() is not very well documented, and there doesn't seem to be a .find_left() method any more.\n\nIt never was because it (along with other functions) is not intended to be used in scripts, only in mappings. Making them work as a standalone functions would be how I'd approach this now, but with current 'mini.surround' that would require a significant rewrite. So I am afraid this won't happen, at least not until there are more reasons to do so.",
